\right)$, where $R$ is the Jordanian $r$-matrix given by $R=1\otimes 1+\alpha r_0$, and $r_0=a\otimes b$ is an infinitesimal Jordanian twist. We demonstrate that there exists a one-parameter family of Jordanian twists $r_0(\lambda)$ that is closed under composition, with the equation $r_0(\lambda_1\circ\lambda_2)=r_0(\lambda_2)\circ\Delta_\alpha(r_0(\lambda_1))$. This family is parameterized by positive integers and given by the explicit formula $r_0(\lambda)=\sum_{n=1}^\lambda\alpha^n\frac{K^n\otimes 1}{n!}$, where $K$ is the Jordanian gauge transformation matrix given by $K=1\otimes 1+\alpha r_1$.
